Fillets: an OnSame end whose blend runs on past the vertex along its
other face, cut along its side by the face at the end (mitcad#343).

A convex edge between a band N and a cone Fo rounded with 1, ending at a
vertex V where a notch wall B (a plane at 8 degrees to the edge) starts:
past V, N goes on as a narrower tongue between the notch walls and Fo
goes on beside B (B's edge with N convex, with Fo concave: an OnSame end).
The bodies stored in the files run the blend on past V along Fo until its
contact on Fo reaches B's edge with Fo (5.9 past V), and B cuts it along
its side from there back to where its contact on N crosses B's plane (4
before V); B grows up to the cut. OCCT walked on past V until the contact
on N left the tongue across its edge with a face tangent to it (4 past V,
the contact on Fo still short of B), and the corner took that edge's face
for the face at the end: an invalid result (faces of reversed orientation)
or two roundings that cross.

Now ChFi3d_Builder::WalkedOnSameToEndFace, after the stripe is walked,
finds such an end (OnSame, a vertex of three edges, the last SurfData past
V with its contact on N on an edge that is not B's and its contact on Fo
inside Fo) and walks that SurfData again from its other end, N's surface
unbounded and the guide run on past its end (the same curve), up to where
the contact on Fo reaches B's edge with Fo; that SurfData replaces the
last one. PerformOneCorner's OnSame corner then cuts it by B and prolongs
B's edge with N up to the contact on N, as for an ordinary OnSame end. The
stripe is left as it was where the walk does not reach that edge. Analytic
blends (not walked) are not changed.

Upstream: new.
